developers to be

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.245
successful in our platform.

00:07:37.245 --> 00:07:38.070
DREA ALFONSO: Cool.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:40.950
So we're here in front
of a wall of pie.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.451
But most importantly, we're
in front of the compute pi

00:07:43.451 --> 00:07:43.950
cruncher.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.810
Tell us what's going
on in front of us here.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.685
TERRENCE RYAN: So one of the key
things about Google Clouds VMs

00:07:48.685 --> 00:07:52.260
is that you can pick very
discrete amounts of processor

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.340
memory.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.000
You don't have to choose between
8 and 16, if what you need

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.980
is 14 processors.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:04.170
So this allows you to spin up a
custom VM to as many processors

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.432
as much memory as you want.

00:08:05.432 --> 00:08:07.140
And we're going to
have it do a job which

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.690
is compute digits of pi.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.130
So we can run this
whole process.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:14.730
And you go from having no VM
to having a that's actually

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.250
done work catcalling
pi, 100 million digits

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:18.600
in usually around a minute.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.290
You can do thing from nothing
to 100 million digits of pi.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.350
TIMOTHY JORDAN: I think that's
just incredible that Google

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.960
Cloud is computing 100
million digits of pi,

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.720
and you're spinning everything
up with just this one

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:31.247
button here.

00:08:31.247 --> 00:08:32.580
TERRENCE RYAN: It's pretty cool.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.419
Our web UI maybe a
little bit more clicks,

00:08:35.419 --> 00:08:38.789
but we could get it down to
just this one button to do that.

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:39.829
It's pretty exciting.

00:08:39.829 --> 00:08:40.770
TIMOTHY JORDAN:
And actually that's

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.990
my favorite thing about
the Google Cloud Platform

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.135
is how easily you can
scale with your business.

00:08:45.135 --> 00:08:47.718
TERRENCE RYAN: That is I think
one of the key differentiators.

00:08:47.718 --> 00:08:49.800
And the fact that
you can make sure you

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.830
get as exactly as many resources
as you need without having

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.210
to go over, you save money.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.120
That's good too.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.140
DREA ALFONSO: So in
addition to the pi cruncher,

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.640
what are some other exciting
things that we should make sure

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.515
