00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:31.500
You know them as the host
of the Google Cloud Podcast.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.851
Here we are with Mark and
Francesc of the GCP podcast.

00:09:34.851 --> 00:09:35.600
How you all doing?

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.641
MARK MANDEL: Doing great.

00:09:36.641 --> 00:09:37.970
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Doing great.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.345
TIMOTHY JORDAN: So why
don't we just start out

00:09:40.345 --> 00:09:42.870
with a very simple and
straightforward question.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.035
What is the podcast?

00:09:46.035 --> 00:09:50.100
MARK MANDEL: So the podcast
is a weekly audio content

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.770
that Francesc and I put
together once a week.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:56.910
And we do interviews with
program managers, engineers,

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.430
customers, a variety
of people across Google

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:02.410
and outside of Google to talk
about how they use Google

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.560
platform and the
lessons they've learned,

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.846
and the cool stuff that they
can tell people about it.

00:10:06.846 --> 00:10:08.986
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah,
sounds pretty much right.

00:10:08.986 --> 00:10:10.360
DREA ALFONSO: In
addition to what

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.630
you guys are doing
with the cloud podcast,

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.905
what else do you guys do here?

00:10:13.905 --> 00:10:16.260
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So we
are developer advocates.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.260
So basically I'd say that
the developer advocate, what

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:26.130
they do is they kind of go
around the world talking

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.420
about Google technology.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:30.090
And then if they hear
good or bad feedback,

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:33.210
they go back to the product
manager and [INAUDIBLE]

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.427
and they get the
feedback back basically.

00:10:35.427 --> 00:10:37.260
MARK MANDEL: I've heard
professional sticker

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.770
distributor,
professional mingler.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.550
DREA ALFONSO:
Stickers are popular.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.175
FRANCESC CAMPOY: We
carry t-shirts too.

00:10:42.175 --> 00:10:42.910
MARK MANDEL: Yeah,
lots of t-shirts.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.330
DREA ALFONSO: You
missed the t-shirt memo.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.510
No, I'm joking.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.307
I'm kidding.

00:10:47.307 --> 00:10:49.140
TIMOTHY JORDAN: Can I
still be at the party?

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.040
So I think developer advocates
do a little more too.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.975
What would you say is your
motto for develop advocacy?

00:10:59.975 --> 00:11:02.190
MARK MANDEL: So for me, I
would say quite literally

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.830
it is our job to
advocate for developers.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.280
It was our job inside Google to
basically go out in the world,

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:10.350
interact with the
external developers who

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.520
use Google platform, and then
be able to be internally be

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.260
able to say, hey, we
represent the interests

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.510
and the experience of
those external developers

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.340
to our internal
product managers,

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.860
especially in engineering,
so that they have

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.480
that sort of conduit
of communication

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.605
to the outside developers.

00:11:25.605 --> 00:11:27.230
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I'd
say in three words

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.432
like make developers happy.

00:11:29.432 --> 00:11:30.765
MARK MANDEL: Love it.

00:11:30.765 --> 00:11:33.450
DREA ALFONSO: And I am assuming
that the podcast is a great way

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:34.580
to reach people.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.330
But how did you guys
come up with the idea

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.625
to do a Google Cloud podcast?

00:11:38.625 --> 00:11:41.790
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So
I've been Google for way

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:42.610
